id: seen
name: Seen
kind: conditions
maxStacks: 1
# Not a Combat Condition: the Intuit entry says the Opponent "becomes 'Seen'", in quotation
# marks, and never calls it one. The same shape as Analyzed, which it is a sibling of.
combatCondition: no
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Somebody has read you. Whoever Seen you rolls better against you in a Clash until the
  end of their next turn.
text: >
  Seen: the Intuit Maneuver's mark. "Target an Opponent, that Opponent becomes 'Seen'
  until the end of your next turn."

---

# The Analyzed mark's sibling, and built the same way for the same reasons.
#
# No effects of its own. What being Seen costs you is written in the Intuit Maneuver,
# because the bonus belongs to whoever Seen you rather than to everybody: "increase the
# Dice Score of YOUR Skill Checks and Saving Throws in Clashes against a Seen Opponent". A
# passive here would hand it to the whole table.
#
# Who read you is the clock. The mark sits on you and the entry timing it sits on them -
# "until the end of YOUR next turn" is their turn - so that entry is both the timer and the
# record of who it was, which is what makes "your Clashes" answerable without a second
# place to keep it.
#
# Not a Combat Condition, so the checklist on the sheet stays the published eighteen. It is
# in this folder because this is where a mark with a clock on it lives.
